The substantially lower CAR on \texttt{spatial\_bowl} relative to \texttt{object\_pudding} (11--12\% vs.\ 54--57\%) reflects the greater scene difficulty: \texttt{spatial\_bowl} places five cluttered obstacles around the workspace, making collision-free manipulation considerably harder. This difficulty affects both conditions equally, and the SDF condition performs comparably ($\Delta$CAR\,=\,$-$0.5\,pp, well within noise), reinforcing the conclusion that EE-only SDF auxiliary supervision does not produce a meaningful collision avoidance benefit beyond LoRA-only fine-tuning.


